Z||000000||LZeitgeist||08-29-2001||11:35 AM||||Has anyone ordered from Mr. Mike's lately? I've been trying to call for the last three days, and every time, it will ring twice, pick up, a voicemail message will come on asking me to hold while they attend other customers, and then the machine hangs up after a ten-second wait. Any ideas? Anyone know if he's out of town at a show or something?I don't want to send my bank card info via e-mail.<P><BR>Also, for those who actually have these, is the #7 Light Grey the closest color to the original grey seat fabric in the '88 notchbacks?  The #8 grey mentions the '88's, while the #7 mentions up to '86, but I'm trying to match the color of the seat fabric rather than the plastic or vinyl interior trim, and I don't trust the actual colors on the monitor. The #8 grey looks much darker on the screen than the #7 grey, and I'm not sure if when he made his notes he was comparing the leather colors to the interior trim or to the original seat fabric. Advice welcomed.<P>------------------<BR>Patrick W. Heinske  --  LZeitgeist@aol.com<BR>1988 Red Fiero Formula<BR>- 1st Place - Stock Coupe - FOCOSEVA 2000<BR>- 3rd Place - Stock Formula - FOCOA Nat'l 2001<p>[This message has been edited by LZeitgeist (edited 08-29-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||Oreif||08-29-2001||11:54 AM||||He has the years slightly off. #7 is 84/85 and #8 is 86-88. #9 matches the dark gray accent of the 84/85 and the dark gray of the dash of all years. Generally when doing 2-tone seats (Like mine, it's an 86) I have #7 inset and #8 for the outside (bolsters/headrest)<P>As for contacting him, Just send him an Email about the phone. Maybe the answering thing in messed up and he doesn't know it.||||reg||1
Z||000002||LZeitgeist||08-29-2001||12:19 PM||||Thanks, Oreif... I guess what I'm asking is this - is the #7 Light Grey the closest color he offers to the color of the seat fabric in the 1988 cloth Formula interior? Or are the colors off on my monitor and I should go with the #8 Grey?<P>I don't want the leather to match the interior parts - I want the leather to be the same color as the original seats in the car. <P>Sorry if my question wasn't clearer the first time... ::smile:: ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Oreif||08-29-2001||12:52 PM||||Yes the #7 is close (not quite exact) to the light gray of the original seats. Sort of like a silver gray.||||reg||1
Z||000004||LZeitgeist||08-29-2001||03:03 PM||||Excellent - sounds perfect. Thanks, Oreif!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
